From d8ed91af02cf668eb4627928d24958b07f3caa18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:51:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Suitability table: use a tighter 100 km label radius

On production data the model's gain over the best simple baseline is only reliable at 100 km
(+0.083 AUC, 95% range +0.029 to +0.136), not at 500 km (+0.036, range -0.021 to +0.094),
because a 500 km circle spans several climates.

- new setting suitability_radius_km: 100 (species_radius_km stays 500 for the older marts)
- crop search moved into macro city_species_presence(radius_km), used by both
  int_city_species_presence and mart_species_city_suitability (old output verified identical)
- cities with no recorded crop inside the circle are left out of the suitability table
- docs and glossary updated

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012HbcbvEafNFn6aR2BmUheY
